// A convenience workspace, and — as of store v1.5.1 — no longer load-bearing.
//
// It used to be committed because without it this repository did not build:
// neither the store module nor runtime-go/cache had a resolvable version, and
// only directory `replace`s made them reachable. Both modules below now resolve
// from the proxy, and `GOWORK=off go build ./... && GOWORK=off go test ./...`
// passes in each of them independently. Keep that true.
//
// What this file still does is group the two modules so an editor and a
// repository-wide `go test ./...` see both at once. Nothing more — there are no
// `replace` directives here, and adding one would quietly float a version that
// go.mod pins.
//
// The one remaining unpublished dependency is runtime-go, which only examples/
// needs; the plugin does not link against the runtime it generates calls into.
// Because runtime-go/cache `replace`s three siblings in its own go.mod — which
// Go ignores in a dependency — examples/go.mod restates those as replaces of its
// own. See the comment there, and docs/boundary-findings.md, finding 5.
go 1.26.5

use (
	.
	./examples
)
